<law>
	<structure>
		<unit label="title" identifier="64.2" level="1">Wills, Trusts, and Fiduciaries</unit>
		<unit label="subtitle" identifier="III" level="2">Trusts</unit>
		<unit label="chapter" identifier="7" level="3">Uniform Trust Code</unit>
		<unit label="article" identifier="5" level="4">Creditor's Claims; Spendthrift and Discretionary Trusts</unit>
	</structure>
	<section_number>64.2-749</section_number>
	<catch_line>Personal obligations of trustee</catch_line>
	<text>
		Trust property is not subject to personal obligations of the trustee, even if the trustee becomes insolvent or bankrupt.
	</text>
	<history>2005, c. 935, § 55-545.07; 2012, c. 614.</history>
</law>
